omponents so you can have  background colors you can have the  website URL and there are some advanced  options as well that you have here you  can have different parameters for your  for your URL which is basically it will  be added to the website URL which  basically means that you could track the  the URL in the your Google Analytics as  well and then you can set up conversion  tracking for your ad as well and we'll  talk about that in more detail in the  next lesson now here you see a very  important aspect of the the answer when  you submit your ad Facebook will review  your ads and will check the the text  will check the image will check the  landing page and if he ad is not good  than and does not comply with the rules  and regulations then Facebook will not  approve your ad and you will get a  message and then you will have to to  change the ads one of the most important  rules in the ad is the 20% textual so  your image may not have more than 20%  stake and here you see that my ad may  reach slightly lower because then there  may be a little bit too much text of the  ad Facebook will not outrightly decline  your ad but it will basically give you a  slightly lower reach if your ad has too  much text and there's more about this  later in the course so then basically  when you're ready you click confirm and  then your ad will go up will be uploaded  to Facebook and then of course Facebook  wants the money so you then need to  enter if you haven't done that yet  you will have to enter your credit or  debit card information so facebook can  take payment  Facebook add images and text Facebook  has a really nice add images cheat sheet  in summary it's all about being  interesting with your image being  focused exciting consistent and fresh  and most important of all make sure  there is a connection between the image  and the message here are a few more tips  on using images in your ads to highlight  a few show people use faces of people  make sure your images are 